# Environment variables for local development.
#
# THIS FILE COVERS THE ADMIN CONSOLE (Vite) ONLY. Copy it to `.env` in the
# repository root — Vite reads `VITE_*` from there at build time. The Expo
# customer app has its own template in a different directory; see the pointer
# below, and do not add EXPO_PUBLIC_* values here.
#
# EVERYTHING PREFIXED `VITE_` OR `EXPO_PUBLIC_` IS COMPILED INTO THE CLIENT
# BUNDLE AND IS PUBLIC. Only ever put credentials here that are designed to be
# public client credentials (CLAUDE.md §9). The Supabase service-role key,
# provider secrets, the Meta app secret and the SMTP password are NOT client
# values: they live in Supabase `integration_settings` / Edge Function secrets
# and must never appear in a `.env` that a bundler can read.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin console (Vite) — src/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase project. The anon key is a public, RLS-scoped credential by design.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="<anon-key>"

# Maps. 'mapbox' or 'google'; each provider needs its own public token/key.
VITE_MAP_PROVIDER="mapbox"
VITE_MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN=""
VITE_MAPBOX_STYLE_URL=""
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=""

# Sentry (surface 'admin-web'). Empty DSN disables reporting entirely.
# Set VITE_SENTRY_DEV=1 to actually send from a local dev server.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=""
VITE_SENTRY_ENV=""
VITE_SENTRY_DEV=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Customer app (Expo) — NOT HERE. See apps/mobile/.env.example
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Expo app does not read this file, and putting EXPO_PUBLIC_* values here
# fails SILENTLY rather than loudly, which is why this section is a pointer
# rather than a list.
#
#   * Expo runs from apps/mobile — apps/mobile/scripts/export-web.js sets
#     `cwd: __dirname + '/..'` — so Metro loads apps/mobile/.env.local and never
#     looks at the repository root.
#   * That same wrapper falls back to a hardcoded PRODUCTION Supabase URL and
#     anon key when the variables are absent. So a value put here is not merely
#     ignored: the build succeeds and quietly targets Production.
#
# Copy the mobile template into place instead, exactly as apps/mobile/README.md
# already says:
#
#     cp apps/mobile/.env.example apps/mobile/.env.local
#
# apps/mobile/.env.example is the authority for the Expo half and is deliberately
# NOT duplicated here. It carries context this file has no business restating —
# which map provider is current, why EXPO_PUBLIC_MAP_WEBVIEW_BASE_URL is
# mandatory for a referrer-restricted Google key, and which existing key to reuse
# rather than mint a second one. A second copy would drift from it, and drifting
# duplicate templates are the reason this file was rewritten in the first place.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time only — set by CI / Vercel, not by you
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERCEL_ENV, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA   Vercel system values; vite.config.ts and
#                                     apps/mobile/scripts/export-web.js alias
#                                     them into VITE_/EXPO_PUBLIC_ build metadata.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN                   OPT-IN source-map upload. When present the
#                                     build emits hidden maps, uploads them, then
#                                     deletes them. SECRET — never commit it.
# DOCS_BASE_REF                       Base ref for scripts/docs-check-ownership.mjs.
# DISABLE_HMR                         Set to "true" to stop Vite watching files.
